{
  "id": "EDU105",
  "title": "The Alarm Reminder Outlasts the Beep",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A resident wants a reliable reminder to check household alarms, but forgets the manufacturer’s maintenance instructions after installation. A reviewed animation links the specific device instructions to a recurring check record without demonstrating repairs.",
  "hook": "Where did the instructions go after the alarm was installed?",
  "visible_action": "A generic alarm icon links to a manual card and dated maintenance record; unverified timing fields stay blank.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Safety-device maintenance should follow the device’s instructions and applicable official guidance.",
  "gate": "Validate alarm type and local guidance; no electrical work, battery substitutions, disabling, or invented intervals. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
